# Android

- Build Falcon components in Jetpack Compose.
- Map color, type, spacing, radius, border, and shadow to tokens in `styles/foundations.css`. Keep raw `Color`, `dp`, and `sp` values out of composables. Use the same names (`brand/500`, `space/4`, `radius/xl`).
- Touch targets are at least 48.dp.
- Meaningful icons set `contentDescription`. Decorative icons use `null`.
- Use Material ripple and system back when they do not change Falcon tokens or component meaning.

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD
Button(colors = ButtonDefaults.buttonColors(containerColor = Color(0xFF009A78)))

// ✅ GOOD
FalconButton(variant = ButtonVariant.Primary, size = ButtonSize.Md)
```
